From fbfe2a22e5b2c57397e5e2587f8d016cd644730c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Jackson <70459+jjackson@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:18:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] Labs runtime: local-disk sandbox dirs, purge on a fresh
 disk, liveness probe, DB pool, HQ read timeout

- Create dbs/ and tmp_dbs/ in the image, and make the nightly temp-db purge a
  no-op when tmp_dbs/ does not exist (it NPE'd in FileUtils.deleteFiles).
- Enable the actuator health probes: /health/liveness reports the JVM only, so a
  container health check on it does not restart the task over a DB/Redis blip.
- spring.jpa.open-in-view=false (JPA_OPEN_IN_VIEW) and explicit Hikari bounds
  (DB_POOL_SIZE=20, DB_CONNECTION_TIMEOUT_MS=10000).
- formplayer.hq.readTimeoutMs (HQ_READ_TIMEOUT_MS), defaulting to upstream's
  15 minutes, for the outbound HQ RestTemplate.
---
