 | `POSTGRESQL_HOST` / `_PORT` / `_DATABASE` / `_USERNAME` / `POSTGRESQL_PASSWROD` (sic) | `spring.datasource.*` | Postgres 10+ holds form/menu sessions, Flyway-migrated on boot. |
 | `REDIS_HOSTNAME` / `REDIS_PASSWORD` / `REDIS_DATABASE` (0) | `redis.*` | Redis holds locks, the CCZ archive index, sync and volatility caches. `REDIS_DATABASE` picks the database index on a standalone Redis, so formplayer can share a server without sharing a keyspace. |
 | `SERVER_PORT` (8080) | `server.port` | API port. |
-| `MANAGEMENT_SERVER_PORT` (8081) | `management.server.port` | `GET /health` (db and redis), `/info`, `/metrics`. Keep it private. |
-| `sqlite.dataDir` (`dbs/`), `sqlite.tmpDataDir` (`tmp_dbs/`) | same | Local disk for per-user and per-app SQLite sandboxes, and the downloaded CCZs. Use a persistent volume; losing it only forces a reinstall and restore. |
+| `MANAGEMENT_SERVER_PORT` (8081) | `management.server.port` | `GET /health` (db and redis), `/health/liveness` (the JVM only: use this for a container health check), `/health/readiness`, `/info`, `/metrics`. Keep it private. |
+| `sqlite.dataDir` (`dbs/`), `sqlite.tmpDataDir` (`tmp_dbs/`) | same | Per-user and per-app SQLite sandboxes, and the downloaded CCZs. A **rebuildable cache**: put it on fast local disk (not network storage, where every SQLite page read is a network round trip). Losing it only forces a reinstall and restore. Both directories exist in the image. |
+| `HQ_READ_TIMEOUT_MS` (900000) | `formplayer.hq.readTimeoutMs` | Read timeout on outbound HQ calls. Upstream's 15 minutes by default; labs runs 60000. |
+| `DB_POOL_SIZE` (20), `DB_CONNECTION_TIMEOUT_MS` (10000) | `spring.datasource.hikari.*` | Postgres pool bounds. |
+| `JPA_OPEN_IN_VIEW` (false) | `spring.jpa.open-in-view` | Off, so a request holds a DB connection only while it uses it. |
 | `SENTRY_DSN`, datadog | optional | |
 
 Build and image: `./gradlew bootJar` (JDK 17) produces `build/libs/formplayer.jar`. Then
